  "overview": "**KERN UX** is a light-first design system anchored on `#f3f4f7` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (17.9:1 contrast) and `brand-colorpalette-1-300` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `Fira Sans` (80px display down to 16px body), unified by `4px` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **Germany Federal Government**. Source: published token package (https://kern-ux.de), package `@kern-ux/native`. Inventory: **91** colors, **26** typography steps, and **30** documented components (EUPL-1.2 license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 30 component tokens with documented paddings: `0rem`, `0`, `0.5rem 1.5rem 1rem 1.5rem`, `0.375rem 0rem 0.125rem 0rem`, `1rem`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#f3f4f7` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`inset 0 -1px 0 0 #6E7597`, `inset 0 -1px 0 0 #6E7597`) paired with `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `brand-colorpalette-1-300` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#f3f4f7` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `brand-colorpalette-1-300` with `#f7f7f8` text (verified) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Fira Sans` headings with `Fira Sans` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `4px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (0.25rem on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#f3f4f7` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `4px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `kern-form-input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
